text.section:
A personal delivery device shall:

Not block any public rights-of-way;


Obey all traffic and pedestrian control devices and signs;


Operate at a speed that does not exceed 10 miles per hour on sidewalks and crosswalks;


Include a unique identifying device number;


Include a means of identifying the personal delivery device operator that is in a position and of such a size to be clearly visible; and


Be equipped with a braking system that, when active or engaged, will enable such personal delivery device to come to a controlled stop.
